<p class="docx-para">OBJECTIVE</p>
<p class="docx-para">To establish documentary evidence to demonstrate that <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_26_blank_0">fill</span> machine I.D No.<span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_26_blank_1">machine id fill</span> located <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_26_blank_2">fill lacated</span> in the facility of Lupin is installed as per the URS <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_26_blank_3">urs fill</span>.and qualified for correct installation and operation as per the guidelines outlined in this protocol &amp;/or operations manual/or qualification provided by the manufacturer/ vendor.</p>
<p class="docx-para">SCOPE</p>
<p class="docx-para">The scope of this document/ is applicable for:</p>
<p class="docx-para">The installation and operational qualification of <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_29_blank_0">qualification of fill</span>. machine I.D <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_29_blank_1">machine id again fill</span> under the following condition/s:</p>
<p class="docx-para docx-para-checkbox"><label class="docx-check-label"><span class="docx-readonly-value" style="display:inline-block;min-width:80px;padding:2px 8px;border-bottom:1px dotted #999;overflow:visible;text-indent:0;white-space:normal;word-break:break-word;"></span> New/ first installation</label></p>
<p class="docx-para docx-para-checkbox"><label class="docx-check-label"><span class="docx-readonly-value" style="display:inline-block;min-width:80px;padding:2px 8px;border-bottom:1px dotted #999;overflow:visible;text-indent:0;white-space:normal;word-break:break-word;"></span> Major modification/ change done after installation</label></p>
<p class="docx-para docx-para-checkbox"><label class="docx-check-label"><span class="docx-readonly-value" style="display:inline-block;min-width:80px;padding:2px 8px;border-bottom:1px dotted #999;overflow:visible;text-indent:0;white-space:normal;word-break:break-word;"></span> Shifted from one location (where installed originally) to another location</label></p>
<p class="docx-para docx-para-checkbox"><label class="docx-check-label"><span class="docx-readonly-value" style="display:inline-block;min-width:80px;padding:2px 8px;border-bottom:1px dotted #999;overflow:visible;text-indent:0;white-space:normal;word-break:break-word;"></span> In Use equipment/system/utility</label></p>
<p class="docx-para">This protocol provides directions/ procedure for identification and verification of the following, leading to qualification for correct installation and operation:</p>
<p class="docx-para">The subjected equipment and its major components</p>
<p class="docx-para">Process control instruments, such as Pressure indicator and Pressure gauge etc.</p>
<p class="docx-para">All product contact surfaces</p>
<p class="docx-para">All Utilities</p>
<p class="docx-para">All product/ process and personnel safety systems</p>
<p class="docx-para">All supporting documentation, such as installation operation and maintenance manuals, parts list and necessary SOP’s.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Operation of all major component / systems.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Operation of the entire equipment as a system.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Operation of process control instrumentation and safety systems.</p>
<p class="docx-para">The protocol also provides directions/ procedure for:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Reporting and handling the deviations observed (if any).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Comparing the as-built and as-installed system with approved design (DQ).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identifying the tentative SOP list with respect to the subjected equipment and providing instructions/ directions for writing the same.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identifying specific personnel training need with respect to its correct operation, cleaning, maintenance or calibration of the equipment and/ or its major components.</p>
<p class="docx-para">RESPONSIBILITY</p>
<p class="docx-para">Responsibilities of different department/ personnel involved in different activities related to the installation and Operational qualification of <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_50_blank_0">procedure for: fill</span>.. machine I.D No. <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_50_blank_1">2 again fill .. machine I.D No.</span>is defined below:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Validation Department</p>
<p class="docx-para">Preparation of IOQ Protocol in consultation with Engineering / Projects if required.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Checking the protocol for accuracy and adequacy prior to the approval.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Preparation of IOQ Summary Report.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Engineering / Production Department</p>
<p class="docx-para">Providing required information to Validation department for preparation of the protocol.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Execution of protocol in-coordination with user department.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Checking the protocol and report for adequacy and accuracy.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Quality Assurance Department</p>
<p class="docx-para">Providing guidance, wherever required to the related departments.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Review and approval of the protocol.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Review and approval of the Installation and Operational qualification Report.</p>
<p class="docx-para">PRE-REQUISITES</p>
<p class="docx-para">Prior to conducting/ executing the installation qualification protocol following conditions must be completed and approved.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Design Qualification Report</p>
<p class="docx-para">EQUIPMENT/ SYSTEM IDENTIFICATION</p>
<p class="docx-para">The subjected equipment/system is identified as <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_68_blank_0">fill he subjected equipment/system is identified</span>. machine I.D No. <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_68_blank_1">fill 3 again  . machine I.D No.</span>. located <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_68_blank_2">fill agai. located</span>.at Facility.</p>
