<p class="docx-para">EQUIPMENT/SYSTEM DESCRIPTION</p>
<p class="docx-para">(Description of the major subsystems if applicable and Description of Major Components):</p>
<p class="docx-para">INSTALLATION CHECKS:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identification of Execution Team Members and Training on Protocol:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Objective: To identify the execution team members and impart training to the personal on the qualification protocol prior to qualification activity.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identify the execution team members from Validation/Engineering / User department / QA and any other related departments as per the requirement.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Training shall be imparted to the personnel involved in execution of qualification protocol. Details of the personnel undergone training and involved on qualification activity shall be recorded in ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097656 (IOQ Attachment 1- Identification of Personnel and Training).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Pre-Installation Checks:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Once the equipment is installed and ready for qualification, following general installation checks shall be conducted and the records enclosed with ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097657 (IOQ Attachment 2 - Pre-installation Checks).</p>
<p class="docx-para">General appearance &amp; equipment identification.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Levelling / Centring / Alignment</p>
<p class="docx-para">Anchoring / Grouting</p>
<p class="docx-para">Access &amp; Clearance</p>
<p class="docx-para">Integration with other equipment</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identification of major components</p>
<p class="docx-para">The major components in the Bundle Machine, those are essential for correct functioning are identified and attached as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097660 (IOQ Attachment 5 - Material of Construction Verification). The major components in the Bundle Machine are identified on the basis of physical inspection, Purchase Order &amp; operation/maintenance manuals.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Main Machine Body</p>
<p class="docx-para">Mechanical Major and Sub Components</p>
<p class="docx-para">Electrical Major and Sub Components</p>
<p class="docx-para">Important details and installation of each major component, identified in this section shall be checked / verified, recorded in a separate Data Sheet and attached as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097658 (IOQ Attachment 3 - Major Components / Sub-systems).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identification and classification of Process Control Instruments and instruments impacting on equipment functionality</p>
<p class="docx-para">All Instruments/Indicators/Sensors provided in the equipment for correct functioning &amp; process control are identified and listed below. The instruments are classified in two categories as (i) Critical (C) for the instruments used to indicate, control or measure the process parameter and (ii) Non Critical (NC) for the instruments which are not used as a part of process control or Instruments shall be classified as per site specific procedure.</p>
