<p class="docx-para">This section will form a basis for development of a calibration program in the future and identification of all instruments, which are required to be calibrated periodically. During the Operational qualification, current calibration status of the Critical (C) class instruments should only be checked, Non-critical (NC) class instruments may be accepted on the basis of the vendor‘s calibration certificate, and shall be calibrated only if found damaged/tampered.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Important details and installation of each instrument identified and classified under this section shall be checked / verified, recorded in a separate Data Sheet and attached as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097659 (IOQ Attachment 4 – Instruments).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Note: If critical class instrument needs to be sent to outside agency for calibration, the calibration certificates of vendor may be considered.</p>
