<p class="docx-para">The contact surfaces identified under this section shall be accepted on the basis of the manufacturer’s material of construction certificate. MOC certificates shall be reviewed and enclosed as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097660.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identification of utilities</p>
<p class="docx-para">The essential Utilities identified under this section shall be verified / checked for installation and the observations shall be recorded and enclosed as Attachment-6.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Power /Electrical connections.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Compressed air connections.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Identification of documents</p>
<p class="docx-para">Each document provided with the equipment shall be identified and attached as enclosures. All documents provided with the equipment shall be critically reviewed and crosschecked with the actual equipment for accuracy.</p>
<p class="docx-para">The list of general documents provided / available with the equipment shall be verified against the requirements specified in the URS / DQ document, the checks recorded and enclosed as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097663 (IOQ Attachment 7 - Identification of Documentation).</p>
<p class="docx-para">If the document is provided () should be indicated on yes option and if the document is not available / not provided a () sign should be indicated on NO option. The location for storage of these documents shall also be written to have a better traceability.</p>
<p class="docx-para">OPERATIONAL CHECKS</p>
<p class="docx-para">Calibration</p>
<p class="docx-para">Reference Calibration Instruments</p>
<p class="docx-para">Calibration Reference Standard Instruments, that are required for calibration of the process control instruments or for verification of certain operating parameters, such as standard tachometer etc. should be in a state of calibration.</p>
<p class="docx-para">The current calibration certificates for the same instruments should clearly provide the reference of NPL traceable standard. These calibration certificates shall be enclosed as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097664 (IOQ Attachment 8 - Instrument Calibration).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Critical Process Control Instruments</p>
<p class="docx-para">The critical instruments identified should be subjected to in-house calibration prior to commencing the OQ tests.</p>
<p class="docx-para">The instruments identified for calibration shall be calibrated in-house or by a contracted agency or as per the corresponding standard operating procedures. Enclose a copy of the calibration certificate provided by the contracted agency or generated in house as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097664.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Test Functions</p>
<p class="docx-para">The test functions are defined as the step-wise unit checks to confirm that each unit/ component in the equipment/ system is functional. When all units/ components in the equipment perform as per the requirement, high level of assurance is established that each unit will perform in unison when the equipment/ system will be operated routinely as per the established SOP.</p>
<p class="docx-para">In order, to evaluate correct functioning/ operation of <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_130_blank_0">dgfdsgd</span> machine, I. D No. <span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="para_130_blank_1">dsfgdsgd</span>.., the following test functions should be checked/ verified as per the defined procedures.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Motor Verification:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Verify the motors in the equipment and record the same in ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097665 (IOQ Attachment 9 - Motors Verification).</p>
<p class="docx-para">Operational, functional, safety and performance checks</p>
<p class="docx-para">In order to evaluate correct functioning/ operation of the equipment, checks such as start-up check, shut down check, operational checks, motor and safety checks shall be performed.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Follow the procedure for checking the functional system as per the Draft SOP prepared before OQ stage and note down the observation in a separate data sheet enclosed as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097666 (IOQ Attachment 10 - Operational / Functional Checks / Safety checks / Performance checks).</p>
<p class="docx-para">INSTALLATION &amp; OPERATIONAL CHECKS/ REVIEW</p>
<p class="docx-para">All check points identified earlier under the section 7.0 and 9.0 shall be crosschecked individually and the observations/ results shall be recorded in a separate data sheet for evaluation. Each Test data sheet shall contain main installation and operation checkpoint, test method/procedure or its reference, observations, results and comments. Each test data sheet shall be reviewed by responsible person and compiled for final evaluation of the system. All check points identified earlier under the section 7.0 and 9.0 shall be crosschecked individually and the observations/ results shall be recorded in a separate data sheet for evaluation. Each Test data sheet shall contain main installation and operation checkpoint, test method/procedure or its reference, observations, results and comments. Each test data sheet shall be reviewed by responsible person and compiled for final evaluation of the system.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Any deviation, exception and / or difference observed with respect to the corresponding acceptance criteria and / or the design as outlined in the URS / DQ document should be adequately discussed and appropriate decision / conclusion to be documented in the corresponding test sheet.</p>
<p class="docx-para">IDENTIFICATION AND VERIFICATION OF STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE</p>
<p class="docx-para">List of SOPs required for correct operation, cleaning, maintenance and calibration shall be identified and recorded in ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097667 (IOQ Attachment 11 – Identification and Verification of SOP’s). Draft SOPs may be prepared before OQ stage (after the completion of IQ). Enclose the prepared draft SOPs along with ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097667.</p>
<p class="docx-para">After successful completion of simulation trials, the draft standard operating procedures prepared shall be verified for its accuracy and completeness. Any changes / corrections required in the draft SOP shall be communicated to the concerned personnel / department and SOP(s) shall be finalized after implementation of the suggested changes.</p>
<p class="docx-para">TRAINING</p>
<p class="docx-para">Training shall be imparted on the SOPs / System and document the same in ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097668 (IOQ Attachment 12 – Training) and enclose the same for reference. The training may include the Operation, Maintenance, Calibration, Cleaning, Safety precautions, Troubleshooting etc.</p>
<p class="docx-para">COMPARISON BETWEEN URS, DQ &amp; IOQ:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Comparison between URS, DQ and IOQ shall be done and recorded in ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097669 (IOQ Attachment 13 - Comparison of URS, DQ &amp; IOQ).</p>
<p class="docx-para">COMPLIANCE OF MITIGATION PLAN IDENTIFIED AT DESIGN REVIEW STAGE</p>
<p class="docx-para">Compliance of mitigation plan identified (if any) shall be verified and recorded ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097670 [(IOQ Attachment 14 - Discussion of IOQ results (IOQ Report)]. Compliance of mitigation plan identified (if any) shall be verified and recorded ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097670 [(IOQ Attachment 14 - Discussion of IOQ results (IOQ Report)].</p>
<p class="docx-para">SUMMARY AND CONCLUSION</p>
<p class="docx-para">On completion of IOQ activity, the data generated shall be collected, compiled, critically reviewed, evaluated; any deviations observed shall be discussed and resolved. Based on the final results and discussions a brief summary (IOQ Report) shall be prepared and shall contain the following:</p>
<p class="docx-para">Objective</p>
<p class="docx-para">Equipment/System Description model and serial number</p>
<p class="docx-para">Observations/ results &amp; evaluation Observations/ results &amp; evaluation</p>
<p class="docx-para">Deviation &amp; corrective actions taken.</p>
<p class="docx-para">Review and Discussion Review and Discussion</p>
<p class="docx-para">Conclusion</p>
<p class="docx-para">The discussion of IOQ results (IOQ Report) shall be enclosed as ANNEX_MUM_CQA_097670.</p>
