<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Blower / motor:</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_1"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_1">Plug type Blower provided in the unit to supply air in the working area, and is directly mount on the motor shaft. The blower recirculates the air by taking the air from the atmosphere and rooms as return air and delivers it to the working areas through supply and return duct. It is capable of developing the static pressure of 135 MM of WC.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Cooling Coil:</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_2"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_2">Cooling coil made up of SS body, copper tube and aluminium fins provided in AHU as a heat exchanger. Cooling coils are generally located in the discharge-air stream, immediately downstream of the mixing plenum and filters to de-humidify the air stream. The supply and return line of chilled water / brine (2 to 8°C) from chiller connected to cooling coil.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Heating Coil:</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_3"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_3">Heating coil made up of SS body, copper tube and aluminium fins is provided in AHU as a heat exchanger. Generally, heating coil is located after cooling coil, so that cooled air passed through the coil and required air condition can be maintain before delivered to the area.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Fresh Air filter</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_4"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_4">The fresh air filter consist of G-4 (10 micron) with the efficiency of 90% down to 10 Micron.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Pre filter</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_5"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_5">The pre filter section consist of F-5 (5-micron) filters with the efficiency of 95% down to 5.0 Micron.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Fine filter</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_6"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_6">The fine filter section should consist of F-8 (3 micron) fine filters with the efficiency of 98% down to 3.0 Micron.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Terminal HEPA Filter</td>
<td class="docx-cell locked" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;background:#F9F9F9;" data-field="table_7_row_7"><span class="docx-readonly-value" data-field="table_7_row_7">Terminal HEPA Filter box consist of 0.3 Micron H-14 HEPA filters. These filters filter the air passed from F-8 (3-micron) fine filter before entering into working area. These filters are not washable and not cleanable.</span></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="docx-cell" style="border:1px solid #000;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:middle;">Bleed Air Filter</td>
